          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Yes — Scoped to the Tab, Debounced, and Position-Only",
        "answer": "The workspace is saved to localStorage under a key established once per browser tab (reused for every later navigation in that tab, not re-scoped per page). It saves each open instance's graphRef, offset, and frame, the active instance, camera position, and shared edges — never the graph content itself, which is always refetched fresh on restore.\n\nSaving is debounced 300ms after any change (opening, closing, moving, panning, zooming — essentially anything that calls the workspace's internal changed() signal).\n\nOn restore, the graph matching the current URL becomes the anchor. Everything else in the saved list comes back as a loading shell that refetches its own content. Focus is never restored from storage — it's always re-derived fresh, landing on the anchor. The saved camera is only trusted if it actually shows the anchor; otherwise the view is reframed to fit the anchor properly, and any instance that ends up nowhere near the resulting view gets relocated next to the anchor instead of left stranded off-screen.",
        "confidence": "high",
        "summary": "The workspace persists to localStorage, scoped to the browser tab, saving positions and references (never content), restored ~300ms after any change.",
        "notes": "Answer reflects the mechanism as fixed during a live debugging session, not the original implementation.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "b902497d-bb23-42ab-8356-53529320aad3"
        },
        "definitionKey": "qa-answer",
