      "data": {
        "title": "The Save Key Follows the Tab, Not the Page",
        "caveat": "The storage key is set once per tab, the first time a graph loads, and every later navigation in that same tab reuses it — even navigating to an unrelated graph. Refreshing after navigating away still restores the original workspace, not a fresh one scoped to whatever you navigated to.",
        "severity": "important",
        "mitigation": "Open a new tab to get workspace persistence scoped to a different starting graph.",
        "notes": "",
