      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Persistent, Tab-Scoped, Position-Only",
        "synthesis": "The workspace survives a reload by saving instance positions, camera state, and graph references (never content) to localStorage, keyed to the browser tab rather than the current page — restored ~300ms after every change, with focus and camera re-derived fresh instead of blindly replayed.",
        "keyPoints": "• Scoped to the tab, not the URL\n• Only positions/references saved, never graph content\n• 300ms debounced auto-save on any change\n• Focus is never restored from storage — the graph matching the current URL becomes focused fresh\n• Camera falls back to fitting the focused graph if the saved one doesn't actually show it",
        "openQuestions": "Should navigating to an unrelated graph in the same tab start a fresh workspace instead of reusing the old one?",
        "notes": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "b902497d-bb23-42ab-8356-53529320aad3"
        },
